  "engines": {
    "node": ">=20"
  },
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "A transit booking system for Kenya's bus/matatu fleet with **dynamic partial-segment seating**: the same physical seat can be sold to multiple passengers for *non-overlapping legs* of the same trip — and each seat is modelled as a **relay chain** (A→B 🔗 B→C 🔗 C→D) so passengers are notified when the seat frees up at their stop. Overlap conflicts are prevented at the database level by a Postgres trigger, so double-booking is impossible even under concurrent requests.",
